+<header><a href="./" class="logo" aria-label="Type Lab home">type<b>/</b>lab<small>A CSS EXPLORER</small></a><div class="header-right"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/font-size-adjust" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the docs ↗</a><span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>Made for the modern web</span></div></header>
+<main>
+<div class="topline"><div><div class="eyebrow"><svg><use href="#type"/></svg>Typography playground</div><h1>Different fonts.<br>Same <span>visual rhythm.</span></h1><p class="intro">A little harmony for your type. Explore how <code>font-size-adjust</code> keeps<br class="desktop-break"> mixed fonts in balance, automatically.</p></div><span class="tiny-note"><svg><use href="#sliders"/></svg> Tweak. Compare. Make it yours.</span></div>
+<div class="workspace">
+<div>
+<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="mixed-title"><div class="panel-head"><div class="panel-title" id="mixed-title"><svg><use href="#type"/></svg>Mixed fonts</div><span class="subtle">One paragraph. Two personalities.</span></div><div class="preview"><div class="preview-top"><span class="tag">THE EVERYDAY MIX</span><span class="live"><span class="dot"></span>Live preview</span></div><p id="mixed-fonts-container">Good typography feels effortless.<br>Even when <code>inline code</code> joins the<br class="desktop-break"> conversation, everything should feel<br class="desktop-break"> like it belongs.</p><div class="legend"><span><i></i><span id="font-legend">DM Sans · regular text</span></span><span><i></i>IBM Plex Mono · inline code</span></div></div><div class="codebar"><code>font-size-adjust: <span id="mixed-code">from-font</span>;</code><button class="copy" data-copy="mixed" aria-label="Copy mixed fonts CSS"><svg><use href="#copy"/></svg><span>Copy CSS</span></button></div></section>
+<section class="panel theme-panel" aria-labelledby="theme-title"><div class="panel-head"><div class="panel-title" id="theme-title"><svg><use href="#sliders"/></svg>Independent theme</div><span class="subtle">Its own style. Its own proportions.</span></div><div id="independent-theme-container" class="theme-preview"><span class="tag" style="color:#9785a5">A DIFFERENT KIND OF CHARACTER</span><h2>A world of its own.</h2><p>This little space plays by its own rules. A serif voice,<br class="desktop-break"> a touch of <code>monospace</code>, and a rhythm all its own.</p><div class="theme-footer"><span class="theme-badge">Georgia + IBM Plex Mono</span><span>Independent x-height ratio</span></div></div><div class="codebar"><code>font-size-adjust: <span id="theme-code">0.52</span>;</code><button class="copy" data-copy="theme" aria-label="Copy independent theme CSS"><svg><use href="#copy"/></svg><span>Copy CSS</span></button></div></section>
+</div>
+<aside class="settings" aria-label="Typography controls"><div class="panel"><div class="settings-head"><svg><use href="#sliders"/></svg>The fine-tuning</div><div class="settings-body"><div class="field"><label class="field-label" for="font-family">Primary font</label><div class="select-wrap"><select id="font-family"><option value="sans">DM Sans</option><option value="arial">Arial</option><option value="verdana">Verdana</option><option value="serif">Georgia</option></select></div><p class="field-note">The starting point for your mixed fonts.</p></div><div class="field"><div class="label-row"><label class="field-label" for="font-size">Font size</label><output for="font-size" id="size-output">26 px</output></div><input id="font-size" type="range" min="18" max="36" value="26" step="1"><div class="range-extents"><span>18 px</span><span>36 px</span></div></div><hr class="divider"><div class="switch-row"><span class="switch-label" id="normalize-label">Normalize font heights</span><button type="button" class="switch" role="switch" aria-checked="true" aria-labelledby="normalize-label" id="normalize"></button></div><p class="field-note">Automatically match the x-height of<br> your primary font.</p><div class="notice"><svg><use href="#info"/></svg><span id="normalize-note">Using <code>from-font</code> to keep regular text and inline code in harmony.</span></div><hr class="divider"><div class="label-row"><label class="field-label" for="theme-ratio">Theme aspect ratio</label><output for="theme-ratio" id="ratio-output">0.52</output></div><input id="theme-ratio" type="range" min="0.4" max="0.7" value="0.52" step="0.01"><div class="range-extents"><span>0.40</span><span>0.70</span></div><p class="field-note">A fixed x-height / font-size ratio.<br>Only affects the independent theme.</p><button class="reset" id="reset"><svg><use href="#reset"/></svg>Reset to defaults</button></div></div><div class="how"><div class="how-title"><svg><use href="#info"/></svg>Small property. Big difference.</div><p>Fonts at the same size don’t always look the same size. <code>font-size-adjust</code> balances their lowercase letter heights, making mixed typography feel more consistent.</p><a class="learn" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/font-size-adjust" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get to know font-size-adjust <span>↗</span></a></div></aside>
+</div>
+<footer><span class="footer-left"><svg><use href="#type"/></svg>Built with curiosity. Styled with modern CSS.</span><span class="footer-right">LESS GUESSWORK. MORE GOOD TYPE.</span></footer>
+</main>
+<script>
+const mixed = document.getElementById('mixed-fonts-container');
+const theme = document.getElementById('independent-theme-container');
+const font = document.getElementById('font-family');
+const size = document.getElementById('font-size');
+const ratio = document.getElementById('theme-ratio');
+const normalize = document.getElementById('normalize');
+const families = {sans:"'DM Sans', Arial, sans-serif", arial:'Arial, sans-serif', verdana:'Verdana, sans-serif', serif:"Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif"};
+function update(){
+  mixed.style.fontFamily = families[font.value];
+  mixed.style.fontSize = `${Number(size.value)/16}rem`;
+  const normalized = normalize.getAttribute('aria-checked') === 'true';
+  mixed.style.fontSizeAdjust = normalized ? 'from-font' : 'none';
+  theme.style.fontSizeAdjust = ratio.value;
+  document.getElementById('size-output').value = `${size.value} px`;
+  document.getElementById('ratio-output').value = Number(ratio.value).toFixed(2);
+  document.getElementById('theme-code').textContent = Number(ratio.value).toFixed(2);
+  document.getElementById('mixed-code').textContent = normalized ? 'from-font' : 'none';
+  document.getElementById('font-legend').textContent = `${font.options[font.selectedIndex].text} · regular text`;
+  document.getElementById('normalize-note').innerHTML = normalized ? 'Using <code>from-font</code> to keep regular text and inline code in harmony.' : 'Normalization is off. Each font now uses its natural proportions.';
+}
+font.addEventListener('change',update);
+size.addEventListener('input',update);
+ratio.addEventListener('input',update);
+normalize.addEventListener('click',()=>{normalize.setAttribute('aria-checked',normalize.getAttribute('aria-checked') !== 'true');update()});
+document.getElementById('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{font.value='sans';size.value='26';ratio.value='0.52';normalize.setAttribute('aria-checked','true');update()});
+document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',async()=>{
+  const isMixed = button.dataset.copy === 'mixed';
+  const css = isMixed ? `#mixed-fonts-container {\n  font-family: ${families[font.value]};\n  font-size: ${Number(size.value)/16}rem;\n  font-size-adjust: ${normalize.getAttribute('aria-checked') === 'true' ? 'from-font' : 'none'};\n}\n#mixed-fonts-container code {\n  font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', Consolas, monospace;\n}` : `#independent-theme-container {\n  font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;\n  font-size-adjust: ${Number(ratio.value).toFixed(2)};\n}`;
+  const label=button.querySelector('span');
+  try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(css);label.textContent='Copied!'}catch{label.textContent='Copy unavailable'}
+  setTimeout(()=>{label.textContent='Copy CSS'},2000);
+}));
+</script>
+</body>
